body:
Alright, I think I understand that in the context of HDR output: games with optional HDR output should simply be designed and built with HDR2D enabled to ensure 2D canvas/GUI elements behave consistently in their transparency blending, regardless of whether HDR output is enabled or not. This is entirely independent of the main topic of this conversation (Glow and Adjustments behaviour with and without HDR2D), but makes it much less important to have these effects behave consistently between HDR2D disabled and enabled, because games with HDR output should have HDR2D enabled to get consistent 2D canvas transparency behaviour anyway.

> the output of the tonemapping shader is either Rec 2020 (when using 2DHDR) or it is tonemapped sRGB otherwise

Super minor thing, but the way I understood how this works is: The output of the tonemapping shader is always post-tonemapped floating point values with sRGB primaries. The difference between HDR2D and is simply that:
- HDR2D enabled produces linear encoded values that will be sRGB encoded and quantized in the blit step
- HDR2D disabled produces nonlinear sRGB encoded values that will be quantized immediately after the tonemapper shader

> Perhaps, I guess when using HDR2D we could convert to sRGB, apply color correction and adjustments, then convert back to Linear. That would require all of our tonemappers to be reversible (I don't think Filmic is reversible though, and maybe not ACES or AGX either).

At this point, it feels like beating a dead horse, but I am hoping to clear up any misunderstandings I may have in my mind: If we disregard the fact that developers would need to change their `Environment` parameters to work with the new appearance and went with one of these options, why would we need to reverse the tonemappers?

**Option A: Linear encoding for Glow and BCS**
(faster performance than `master`)
``` diff
diff --git a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/tonemap.glsl b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/tonemap.glsl
index 3043dae8bc..2bc1c7906b 100644
--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/tonemap.glsl
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/tonemap.glsl
@@ -866,9 +866,6 @@ void main() {

        color.rgb = apply_tonemapping(color.rgb, params.white);

-       if (bool(params.flags & FLAG_CONVERT_TO_SRGB)) {
-               color.rgb = linear_to_srgb(color.rgb); // Regular linear -> SRGB conversion.
-       }
 #ifndef SUBPASS
        // Glow
        if (bool(params.flags & FLAG_USE_GLOW) && params.glow_mode != GLOW_MODE_MIX) {
@@ -879,9 +876,6 @@ void main() {

                // high dynamic range -> SRGB
                glow = apply_tonemapping(glow, params.white);
-               if (bool(params.flags & FLAG_CONVERT_TO_SRGB)) {
-                       glow = linear_to_srgb(glow);
-               }

                color.rgb = apply_glow(color.rgb, glow);
        }
@@ -893,6 +887,10 @@ void main() {
                color.rgb = apply_bcs(color.rgb, params.bcs);
        }

+       if (bool(params.flags & FLAG_CONVERT_TO_SRGB)) {
+               color.rgb = linear_to_srgb(color.rgb); // Regular linear -> SRGB conversion.
+       }
+
        if (bool(params.flags & FLAG_USE_COLOR_CORRECTION)) {
                color.rgb = apply_color_correction(color.rgb);
        }
```

**Option B: Nonlinear sRGB encoding for Glow and BCS**
(slowest performance)
``` diff
diff --git a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/tonemap.glsl b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/tonemap.glsl
index 3043dae8bc..72f5c214fa 100644
--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/tonemap.glsl
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/tonemap.glsl
@@ -328,12 +328,15 @@ vec3 tonemap_agx(vec3 color) {
 }

 vec3 linear_to_srgb(vec3 color) {
-       //if going to srgb, clamp from 0 to 1.
-       color = clamp(color, vec3(0.0), vec3(1.0));
        const vec3 a = vec3(0.055f);
        return mix((vec3(1.0f) + a) * pow(color.rgb, vec3(1.0f / 2.4f)) - a, 12.92f * color.rgb, lessThan(color.rgb, vec3(0.0031308f)));
 }

+vec3 srgb_to_linear(vec3 color) {
+       const vec3 a = vec3(0.055f);
+       return mix(pow((color.rgb + a) / (vec3(1.0f) + a), vec3(2.4f)), color.rgb / 12.92f, lessThan(color.rgb, vec3(0.04045f)));
+}
+
 #define TONEMAPPER_LINEAR 0
 #define TONEMAPPER_REINHARD 1
 #define TONEMAPPER_FILMIC 2
@@ -866,9 +869,7 @@ void main() {

        color.rgb = apply_tonemapping(color.rgb, params.white);

-       if (bool(params.flags & FLAG_CONVERT_TO_SRGB)) {
-               color.rgb = linear_to_srgb(color.rgb); // Regular linear -> SRGB conversion.
-       }
+       color.rgb = linear_to_srgb(color.rgb); // Regular linear -> SRGB conversion.
 #ifndef SUBPASS
        // Glow
        if (bool(params.flags & FLAG_USE_GLOW) && params.glow_mode != GLOW_MODE_MIX) {
@@ -879,9 +880,7 @@ void main() {

                // high dynamic range -> SRGB
                glow = apply_tonemapping(glow, params.white);
-               if (bool(params.flags & FLAG_CONVERT_TO_SRGB)) {
-                       glow = linear_to_srgb(glow);
-               }
+               glow = linear_to_srgb(glow);

                color.rgb = apply_glow(color.rgb, glow);
        }
@@ -903,5 +902,9 @@ void main() {
                color.rgb += screen_space_dither(gl_FragCoord.xy);
        }

+       if (!bool(params.flags & FLAG_CONVERT_TO_SRGB)) {
+               color.rgb = srgb_to_linear(color.rgb);
+       }
+
        frag_color = color;
 }
```

